's also `/notes/:id` which would match `/notes/search`. If the `:id` route is defined before the search routes, then `/notes/search` would be matched by `/notes/:id` with `id = \"search\"`. I need to make sure the search routes are defined BEFORE the `/notes/:id` route.\n\nLooking at the current routes.ts:\n1. GET /notes\n2. GET /notes/:id\n3. POST /notes\n4. PUT /notes/:id\n5. DELETE /notes/:id\n\nI need to add the search routes BEFORE `/notes/:id` to avoid the `:id` parameter matching \"search\" or \"search/suggest\".\n\nLet me now implement everything.\n\nFor the FTS5 query sanitization, I'll create a helper function in routes.ts.\n\nLet me write the code:\n\n```typescript\n// db.ts changes - add after CREATE TABLE notes\n\ndb.exec(`\n  CREATE VIRTUAL TABLE IF NOT EXISTS notes_fts USING fts5(title, body);\n  \n  CREATE TRIGGER IF NOT EXISTS notes_fts_insert AFTER INSERT ON notes BEGIN\n    INSERT INTO notes_fts(rowid, title, body) VALUES (new.id, new.title, new.body);\n  END;\n  \n  CREATE TRIGGER IF NOT EXISTS notes_fts_update AFTER UPDATE ON notes BEGIN\n    INSERT INTO notes_fts(notes_fts, rowid, title, body) VALUES ('delete', old.id, old.title, old.body);\n    INSERT INTO notes_fts(rowid, title, body) VALUES (new.id, new.title, new.body);\n  END;\n  \n  CREATE TRIGGER IF NOT EXISTS notes_fts_delete AFTER DELETE ON notes BEGIN\n    INSERT INTO notes_fts(notes_fts, rowid, title, body) VALUES ('delete', old.id, old.title, old.body);\n  END;\n`);\n```\n\nWait, but the seed function inserts notes directly into the `notes` table. With the triggers in place, the FTS table should be automatically populated when seed data is inserted. Good.\n\nBut wait, the CRUD tests in notes.test.ts insert notes directly using `appCtx.db.prepare(\"INSERT INTO notes ...\")`. With triggers, these should also populate the FTS table. Good.\n\nNow let me think about the search route handler:\n\n```typescript\n// GET /notes/search\nrouter.get('/notes/search', (req: Request, res: Response, next: NextFunction) => {\n  try {\n    const q = req.query.q as string | undefined;\n    \n    if (!q || q.trim() === '') {\n      throw new ValidationError('Search query is required');\n    }\n    \n    const page = Math.max(1, parseInt(req.query.page as string) || 1);\n    const perPage = 20;\n    const offset = (page - 1) * perPage;\n    \n    const ftsQuery = buildFTSQuery(q);\n    \n    // Get total count\n    const countStmt = db.prepare(`SELECT COUNT(*) as total FROM notes_fts WHERE notes_fts MATCH ?`);\n    const { total } = countStmt.get(ftsQuery) as { total: number };\n    \n    // Get paginated results\n    const stmt = db.prepare(`\n      SELECT \n        notes.id,\n        notes.title,\n        snippet(notes_fts, 1, '<mark>', '</mark>', '...', 20) as snippet,\n        rank\n      FROM notes_fts\n      JOIN notes ON notes.id = notes_fts.rowid\n      WHERE notes_fts MATCH ?\n      ORDER BY rank\n      LIMIT ? OFFSET ?\n    `);\n    \n    const results = stmt.all(ftsQuery, perPage, offset) as SearchResult[];\n    \n    res.json({ results, total, page, perPage });\n  } catch (err) {\n    next(err);\n  }\n});\n```\n\nAnd the suggest route:\n```typescript\n// GET /notes/search/suggest\nrouter.get('/notes/search/suggest', (req: Request, res: Response, next: NextFunction) => {\n  try {\n    const q = req.query.q as string | undefined;\n    \n    if (!q || q.trim() === '') {\n      throw new ValidationError('Search prefix is required');\n    }\n    \n    // Sanitize prefix - only keep alphanumeric\n    const prefix = q.replace(/[^\\p{L}\\p{N}]/gu, '');\n    \n    if (!prefix) {\n      res.json({ results: [] });\n      return;\n    }\n    \n    const stmt = db.prepare(`\n      SELECT notes.id, notes.title\n      FROM notes_fts\n      JOIN notes ON notes.id = notes_fts.rowid\n      WHERE notes_fts MATCH ?\n      ORDER BY rank\n      LIMIT 5\n    `);\n    \n    const results = stmt.all(`${prefix}*`) as SuggestResult[];\n    \n    res.json({ results });\n  } catch (err) {\n    next(err);\n  }\n});\n```\n\nNow I need the `buildFTSQuery` function:\n```typescript\nfunction buildFTSQuery(query: string): string {\n  const parts: string[] = [];\n  \n  // Extract quoted phrases\n  const phraseRegex = /\"([^\"]+)\"/g;\n  let match;\n  let remaining = query;\n  \n  while ((match = phraseRegex.exec(query)) !== null) {\n    parts.push(`\"${match[1]}\"`);\n    remaining = remaining.replace(match[0], ' ');\n  }\n  \n  // Process remaining unquoted terms\n  // Strip non-alphanumeric characters (keep unicode letters/numbers and spaces)\n  remaining = remaining.replace(/[^\\p{L}\\p{N}\\s]/gu, ' ');\n  const terms = remaining.split(/\\s+/).filter(t => t.length > 0);\n  \n  // Add terms as simple tokens (FTS5 will match them)\n  parts.push(...terms);\n  \n  return parts.join(' ');\n}\n```\n\nWait, but what about the special characters test? Let me trace through:\n1. `hello world` → remaining = `hello world` (no quotes), terms = ['hello', 'world'], result = 'hello world'\n2. `test&test` → remaining = `test test`, terms = ['test', 'test'], result = 'test test' (duplicate, but FTS5 handles it)\n3. `it's` → remaining = `it s`, terms = ['it', 's'], result = 'it s'\n4. `<script>` → remaining = `script`, terms = ['script'], result = 'script'\n5. `foo+bar` → remaining = `foo bar`, terms = ['foo', 'bar'], result = 'foo bar'\n6. `a/b` → remaining = `a b`, terms = ['a', 'b'], result = 'a b'\n\nAll of these should work with FTS5 MATCH. The 'it s' query would match documents with both 'it' and 's', which is fine. The 'a b' query might match many documents, but that's okay.\n\nWait, actually FTS5 has a minimum token length. Single character tokens might not be indexed by default. Let me check... Actually, FTS5 does index single characters by default. So 'a' and 'b' should work.\n\nBut 's' might not return any meaningful results. That's fine - the test just expects a 200 status and an array.\n\nHmm, but wait. The test expects `res.status` to be 200 for all t